Modifications (branch `falcon`, from upstream commit ec4a671), made in 2026 by
Justin Schnettler, adapt the app to XbotGo Falcon youth-soccer recordings:

  * modules/falcon/ (new): Falcon .mark / .vdata support, the marks-only and
    hybrid clip plans, parent taps as a scoring signal, numpy-only camera-pan
    compensation, a low-resolution analysis proxy for 4K/HEVC, phone-friendly
    exports (1080p, vertical, letterbox, loudness normalisation), a
    falcon-soccer preset, and a `python -m modules.falcon` command line.
  * modules/segments/motion_scene_detect_optimized.py: optional camera-motion
    compensation (`camera_compensation`).
  * pipeline.py: the parent-tap signal, Falcon marks/hybrid plans, the proxy
    and compensation switches.
  * modules/media/video_cache.py, modules/report/highlight_report.py,
    video_ai_editor/signal_timeline.py, signal_timeline_viewer.py, main.py,
    sidecar/server.py, mcp_server/: wiring for the above ("Parent tap" in the
    report and on the timeline, the `falcon:` config section, a /falcon/plan
    route and a falcon_plan MCP tool).
  * tests/test_falcon_*.py (new), tests/test_mcp_server.py (one tool added).
  * docs/FALCON.md, requirements-falcon-lite.txt (new).

Parts of modules/falcon/ are ported from falcon-hypecut, the same author's
own Apache-2.0 project, and are distributed here under the AGPL-3.0-or-later
as part of this work.

